{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Narrower reproduction, 2026-11-04 PST, macOS: on base b7c6ed6c834 (no local changes), running only tests/interfaces/facades/test_plan_review_attestation_facades.py and tests/interfaces/facades/test_verify_completion_facades.py with -n 4 fails both tests 2 of 2 times (27 passed, 2 failed), each with the same '--- Logging error --- ValueError: I/O operation on closed file' stderr prefix. Run alone as a pair without xdist, test_cli_passed_but_unsigned_is_exit_11_with_byte_identical_stderr passed and test_cli_llm_error_is_clean_exit_one failed. So the leaking handler comes from within those 2 modules, not from elsewhere in the tree. Found while verifying soot-ammonitic-redpoll."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793825569226397001,"uuid":"6142d702-01a5-415e-9c08-185ebcd180c7"}